  {
   "id": "person.pons",
   "facts": [{"id": "fact.pons_debts", "text": "Owes money all over the Arenal, they say: Grilo most of all."}, {"id": "fact.pons_almara", "text": "Left Almara after a patient of good family died under his knife; he says the man was dead before he came."}],
   "conversation": {"first": "The barber-surgeon's eyes go past you to the street before they come back. \"Captain. Forgive me. I thought you were someone else.\"", "again": "\"Captain.\" Pons glances over your shoulder again, out of habit.", "topics": [{"id": "topic.pons.trade", "ask": "What can you do for a crew?", "says": "\"Bleed them, purge them, set their bones, draw their teeth, sew them up when they fall out of the rigging. I have treated the flux on three ships and lost fewer than any surgeon you will find in this town.\" He shows you his case: the instruments are clean and well kept, which is more than his coat is.", "claims": {"skill.first_aid": 5, "skill.surgery": 4}, "trust": 3}, {"id": "topic.pons.flux", "ask": "And the flux, at sea?", "after": ["topic.pons.trade"], "says": "\"Bad water and bad pork, Captain, and men who drink from the same cup. Buy your water from Gil, not the Brennish fellow; I would put a guard on the cask myself. If it comes aboard anyway, I can keep most of them alive.\"", "respect": 4, "trust": 3}, {"id": "topic.pons.watching", "ask": "Who are you watching for?", "after": ["topic.pons.trade"], "says": "He laughs, not well. \"Creditors, Captain. A surgeon's patients pay when they live and their widows never do. I would like to be at sea before certain gentlemen find me, I said so.\"", "guard": {"trust": 6, "says": "\"No one. The street is busy.\" He smiles and does not mean it.", "change": -2}, "tells": ["fact.pons_debts"], "trust": 4}, {"id": "topic.pons.grilo", "ask": "I saw Grilo with you. How much do you owe him?", "known": ["fact.pons_creditor"], "says": "Pons wets his lips. \"Four hundred. He will be at the gangway for it if you sign me on; he has done it to better men. I would pay him from my advance if I could, Captain, but then I would sail with nothing for my family.\"", "trust": 5}, {"id": "topic.pons.almara", "ask": "Why did you leave Almara?", "after": ["topic.pons.watching"], "says": "\"A merchant's son with a ball in his belly. He was dead before they carried him to me, and his father said I killed him. In Almara the father is believed.\" He shrugs. \"I came here. Here I am believed by no one, which is better.\"", "guard": {"trust": 12, "says": "\"For the sea air.\" He holds your eye for a moment too long.", "change": -3}, "tells": ["fact.pons_almara"], "trust": 6, "affection": 4}, {"id": "topic.pons.terms", "ask": "What would you want for the voyage?", "seeking": true, "terms": true, "after": ["topic.pons.trade"], "says": "\"Thirteen hundred in advance. A surgeon's chest has to be filled before it sails, and nothing in it is cheap.\""}]},
