  {
   "id": "person.bartolo",
   "song": {"voice": "man", "title": "The Caulkers' Song", "says": "Old Bartolo sings a yard song from when he was a boy, tapping the beat on the table with his knuckles like a caulking mallet. Only the old men know the words. They sing them with their eyes shut.", "lines": ["Oakum in the seam, boys, pitch upon the oakum,", "and the sea will never find the way into her bosom..."]},
   "conversation": {"first": "The old carpenter straightens from his work slowly, one hand in the small of his back. \"Captain. They say you want a carpenter who knows a caravel. Well. I knew the Garza when she was built.\"", "again": "Bartolo wipes his hands on his apron. \"Captain.\"", "topics": [{"id": "topic.bartolo.garza", "ask": "You knew the Garza when she was built?", "says": "\"Forty years ago, in the yard where Benito has his forge now. Oak from the hills, the good oak, before they cut it all. She has a soft plank under the larboard bow; she always had. I can show you where.\"", "claims": {"skill.ship_repair": 5, "skill.carpentry": 4}, "trust": 4, "respect": 3}, {"id": "topic.bartolo.age", "ask": "Are you not too old for another voyage?", "after": ["topic.bartolo.garza"], "says": "He does not take offence. \"Too old to go aloft. Too old to haul. Not too old to know which seam is going to open before it opens, and that is what you pay a carpenter for. Pay a young one to swing the maul.\"", "respect": 4}, {"id": "topic.bartolo.wife", "ask": "Will anyone mind you going?", "after": ["topic.bartolo.garza"], "says": "\"My wife is in the churchyard. My sons are in Lusara and do not write.\" He looks at the Garza for a while. \"Father Anselmo will mind. He will have no one left to argue with.\"", "affection": 6, "trust": 4}, {"id": "topic.bartolo.gil", "ask": "Who else should I take?", "after": ["topic.bartolo.garza"], "says": "\"Gil, the cooper. A ship's water is only as good as her casks, and his do not leak. And if you want a cook, Nuño at the Three Anchors, if Inés will let him go, which she will not.\"", "trust": 2}, {"id": "topic.bartolo.terms", "ask": "What would you want?", "seeking": true, "terms": true, "after": ["topic.bartolo.garza"], "says": "\"Eleven hundred, and room in the hold for my tool chest. My own tools. I do not work with the Company's.\""}]},
