  {
   "id": "person.leonor",
   "conversation": {"first": "The young widow does not get up. She finishes the line she is writing, blots it, and only then looks at you. \"You will be the Garza's captain. Micer Varzi said you would come to me.\"", "again": "Leonor closes the ledger on her finger. \"Captain.\"", "topics": [{"id": "topic.leonor.husband", "ask": "Your husband was at Punta Ceniza?", "says": "\"Tomás. The factor's clerk, four years. He kept the factory's books, and he kept a copy, which no one at the Company knows but me.\" She taps the ledger. \"He died of the fever last spring. He is owed a share of every cargo that went through his hands, and they mean to forget it.\"", "claims": {"skill.negotiation": 3}, "trust": 4}, {"id": "topic.leonor.books", "ask": "What use are the books to me?", "after": ["topic.leonor.husband"], "says": "\"The factor at Punta Ceniza will tell you what the Company is owed and what it has. I can tell you whether he is lying. Most of them are, a little. Some of them a great deal.\"", "respect": 6}, {"id": "topic.leonor.sailors", "ask": "The crew will not like a woman aboard.", "after": ["topic.leonor.husband"], "says": "\"No. Nor a clerk, nor a widow, nor anyone who can read their articles back to them.\" For the first time she almost smiles. \"I have been not liked by better men than your topman, Captain.\"", "affection": 4, "respect": 3}, {"id": "topic.leonor.terms", "ask": "What would you want for the passage?", "seeking": true, "terms": true, "after": ["topic.leonor.husband"], "says": "\"Six hundred, and a place to keep the ledger dry. I will work for it: the Garza's own books, and the purser's if you have none.\""}]},
