  {
   "id": "person.tome",
   "facts": [{"id": "fact.tome_sailor", "text": "Was a sailor once, they say, on a ship that came home without her master."}, {"id": "fact.tome_master", "text": "Says the master of the Caridad beat a ship's boy to death, and the crew put him over the side; he was one of them."}],
   "conversation": {"first": "The big man in irons looks at you, then at the guards, then at you again. \"You're the one taking convicts? Captain. I'll pull anything you like.\"", "again": "Tomé shifts his weight; the chain between his ankles clinks. \"Captain.\"", "topics": [{"id": "topic.tome.pardon", "ask": "What did they take you up for?", "says": "\"A knifing on the waterfront. He came at me first, but he had friends and I had none.\" He holds up his wrists. \"The pardon is if I sail, and stay on the coast a year. I'll stay two.\"", "trust": 4}, {"id": "topic.tome.sea", "ask": "Have you been to sea?", "after": ["topic.tome.pardon"], "says": "\"Never, Captain. But I can pull and lift.\" He says it a little too quickly.", "claims": {"skill.sailing": 0, "skill.seamanship": 0}}, {"id": "topic.tome.caridad", "ask": "Mateo says you were a sailor once.", "known": ["fact.tome_sailor"], "says": "He looks at the stones for a long time. \"The Caridad. Her master beat the ship's boy to death in the Lusaran roads, for spilling his wine. We put him over the side that night, all of us. I knew the boy's mother.\" He lifts his chin. \"Hang me for it if you like. I can hand, reef and steer, Captain. I didn't lie to get aboard; I lied to stay alive.\"", "guard": {"trust": 8, "says": "\"Mateo says a lot of things for a man who stands in one place all day.\" His hands tighten on the chain.", "change": -3}, "tells": ["fact.tome_master"], "claims": {"skill.sailing": 3, "skill.seamanship": 3}, "trust": 8, "affection": 4}, {"id": "topic.tome.terms", "ask": "What do you want, besides the pardon?", "seeking": true, "terms": true, "after": ["topic.tome.pardon"], "says": "\"A hundred and fifty, for my mother. That's all. The pardon is the pay.\""}]},
   "farewell": "The guard unlocks Tomé's irons at the foot of the gangway and hands up his pardon. Tomé holds it as if it might blow away.",
