  {
   "id": "person.nuno",
   "song": {"voice": "kitchen", "title": "Garlic and Onions", "says": "Nuño comes out of the kitchen with a ladle and bangs the time on a pot. It is a cook's song with a chorus everyone knows, and everyone shouts it, the dockers loudest. Inés pretends to be cross.", "lines": ["Garlic for the sailor, onions for the priest,", "and the cook gets the bottom of the pot at least!"]},
   "conversation": {"first": "The cook comes out wiping his hands, smelling of onions. \"Captain! Sit, sit. Inés says you're looking for a cook, and you've come to the only one worth having.\"", "again": "\"Captain! Hungry?\" Nuño is already reaching for a bowl.", "topics": [{"id": "topic.nuno.cooking", "ask": "What can you do with ship's stores?", "says": "\"Biscuit, pork, peas, oil, a bit of garlic. Most cooks boil it and call it dinner. I make it so a man looks forward to it, and a man who looks forward to his dinner does his watch.\" He presses a bowl on you: it is good.", "claims": {"skill.cooking": 4}, "trust": 5, "affection": 4}, {"id": "topic.nuno.ines", "ask": "Will Inés let you go?", "after": ["topic.nuno.cooking"], "says": "He looks back at the kitchen door. \"Five years I've cooked for her. She'll shout. Then she'll find someone who boils it.\" Quieter: \"I was at sea before I was a cook, Captain. I'd like to see it again before I'm too fat for the hatch.\"", "affection": 4, "trust": 3}, {"id": "topic.nuno.talk", "ask": "What do you hear, in the kitchen?", "after": ["topic.nuno.cooking"], "says": "\"Everything Inés hears, a little later and with more onions.\" He leans in. \"Pons the barber owes Grilo more than his coat is worth. And the young topman Rodrigo has told every girl on the waterfront he is sailing on the Garza.\"", "trust": 2}, {"id": "topic.nuno.terms", "ask": "What would you want?", "seeking": true, "terms": true, "after": ["topic.nuno.cooking"], "says": "\"Five hundred, and a proper fire box, lined, not a sandbox on the deck. I'll not set your ship alight, Captain.\""}]},
   "farewell": "Inés stands in the tavern door with her arms folded and does not wave to Nuño. Then she does.",
