  {
   "id": "person.ulloa",
   "facts": [{"id": "fact.ulloa_corvera", "text": "Lost a company of soldiers at Corvera through pride, says Varzi."}, {"id": "fact.ulloa_son", "text": "Had a son in the company at Corvera, who did not come back."}],
   "conversation": {"first": "The gentleman inclines his head exactly as far as a gentleman should to a ship's captain. \"Don Fernán de Ulloa. You will have heard that I wish to buy a passage.\"", "again": "\"Captain.\" Don Fernán's hand rests on his sword hilt, as it always does.", "topics": [{"id": "topic.ulloa.passage", "ask": "Why does a gentleman want passage to the Ember Coast?", "says": "\"For the same reason as every other gentleman on that coast: there is nothing left for him at home.\" He says it lightly. \"I have commanded men. You will find that useful, the day your sailors stop listening to you.\"", "claims": {"skill.leadership": 4}, "respect": 2}, {"id": "topic.ulloa.sea", "ask": "Have you been to sea?", "after": ["topic.ulloa.passage"], "says": "\"Across the strait, twice.\" A pause. \"In good weather.\"", "claims": {"skill.navigation": 2}, "affection": 2}, {"id": "topic.ulloa.corvera", "ask": "Varzi says you lost a company at Corvera.", "known": ["fact.ulloa_corvera"], "says": "For a moment he is very still. \"I was told to hold the bridge, and I held it, after any sensible man would have given it up. Ninety men. My son was the ensign.\" He looks at you with no expression at all. \"I do not need the Ligurese to tell my story, Captain. But now you know it.\"", "guard": {"trust": 10, "says": "\"Micer Varzi counts money. He should keep to it.\" His knuckles are white on the hilt.", "change": -6}, "tells": ["fact.ulloa_son"], "trust": 8, "respect": 6}, {"id": "topic.ulloa.terms", "ask": "What will you pay, for the passage?", "seeking": true, "terms": true, "after": ["topic.ulloa.passage"], "says": "\"Four hundred, and I bring my own sword and my own food. I will not mess with the sailors.\""}]},
