  {
   "id": "person.grilo",
   "conversation": {"first": "The moneylender's boy holds the ledger open before Grilo has said a word. \"Captain. You have the look of a man about to spend a great deal of money. Sit down.\"", "again": "\"Captain.\" Grilo smiles; the boy opens the ledger.", "topics": [{"id": "topic.grilo.pons", "ask": "Pons the barber owes you money?", "says": "\"Four hundred sueldos, since Candlemas. The best surgeon in the Arenal and the worst payer. If he sails with you, Captain, I will want my money from his wages, at the gangway, before he goes up it.\"", "trust": 1, "about": "person.pons", "tells": ["fact.pons_debts"]}, {"id": "topic.grilo.loan", "ask": "Would you lend to the Garza?", "says": "\"To the Garza? At the Company's risk, at thirty in the hundred. To you, Captain? Come back when the whole quay knows your name.\" He spreads his ringed hands. \"It is not personal.\""}]},
   "claim": {"debtor": "person.pons", "amount": 400, "says": "\"You have signed on Pons, the barber. He owes me four hundred sueldos, Captain, and I will have it from his advance before he sails, or the Chamber will hear of it.\"", "atGangway": "\"Four hundred sueldos, Captain. Pons does not go up that plank until I have them.\""},
