  {
   "id": "person.andres",
   "song": {"voice": "chorus", "title": "Heave and Bring Her Home", "says": "Andrés starts a capstan shanty, the way a bosun does, and half the room answers the calls without thinking: anyone who has been to sea. You can tell who has and who has not by who knows when to stamp.", "lines": ["Heave and bring her home, my lads, heave and bring her home,", "the wind is in the west, my lads, and the girls are all alone!"]},
   "conversation": {"first": "The scarred docker sets down his load and straightens, favouring one knee. \"Captain. You'll be wanting a bosun, I suppose, and you'll be wanting a younger one than me.\"", "again": "Andrés nods. \"Captain.\"", "topics": [{"id": "topic.andres.knee", "ask": "What happened to the knee?", "says": "\"A block came down off the main yard in the Lusaran roads. Fifteen years a bosun, and one bad splice.\" He shrugs. \"I haul bales now. It's dry work.\"", "affection": 3, "trust": 3}, {"id": "topic.andres.rodrigo", "ask": "What do you make of the topman Rodrigo?", "says": "\"Quick aloft, I'll give him that. Talks a good deal more than he knows. Put him under a bosun who'll knock it out of him and he'll be a fine seaman in two years.\"", "trust": 2}, {"id": "topic.andres.crew", "ask": "What would you look for, in a crew?", "after": ["topic.andres.knee"], "says": "\"Men who've been wet before. A cook they like and a carpenter who's old enough to be careful. And no two men who hate each other in the same watch: you'll have your topman and the Brennish lad at each other's throats by the cape.\"", "respect": 4, "trust": 3}]},
